{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833691-entering-the-umbra","id":833691,"title":"Entering the Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-19T20:56:36-08:00","id":833691,"title":"Entering the Umbra","content":"So a player and I had a small disagreement on something so I wanted to see what others on here think. I always imagined that to enter the umbra you had to actually be able to move, could have sworn this was stated and I'e always seen it in art and well the term &quot;side stepping&quot;. My player argues W20 doesn't mention movement at all and it states &quot;meditation&quot; which she argues is usually done while standing still. Thoughts? This came up while she was grappled by a rather strong Nosferatu and she has Pulse the Invisible, she wanted to side step to break free of the grip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:32:08-08:00","id":833707,"title":"","content":"I would say no either way, how in a heated combat could she not only find the calm but the focus to step sideways and not get crushed while she attempted? <br /> <br /> I only allow the spending of a point to go across in a calm relaxed situation btw. <br /> <br /> As for moving or standing still I rule it off how thick the gauntlet is, try going in a science lab and it's clawing and digging, middle of a forest it's but a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T00:27:11-08:00","id":833742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833691-entering-the-umbra#post833691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a player and I had a small disagreement on something so I wanted to see what others on here think. I always imagined that to enter the umbra you had to actually be able to move, could have sworn this was stated and I'e always seen it in art and well the term &quot;side stepping&quot;. My player argues W20 doesn't mention movement at all and it states &quot;meditation&quot; which she argues is usually done while standing still. Thoughts? This came up while she was grappled by a rather strong Nosferatu and she has Pulse the Invisible, she wanted to side step to break free of the grip.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... if the player had their way, as long as the gauntlet isn't too high, Garou are effectively immune to being grappled? That seems quite silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T06:54:04-08:00","id":833808,"title":"","content":"I agree with the general sentiment, since crossing is not exactly something that's easy to do. I might allow it under stresfull conditions, but it would increase the difficulty, and most likely slow you quite down in your traversing the Gauntlet (Which will probably cause problems of its own)<br /> <br /> How does Pulse of the Invisible pertain to this situation? It just allows you to see into the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T09:56:27-08:00","id":833890,"title":"","content":"Pulse the invisible in w20 makes it so no reflective surface is required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T12:02:45-08:00","id":833963,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would increase the difficulty of the role due to stress/distractions, but I would allow the player to try to side step. I think traditionally that Garou start out learning to step sideways by actually stepping into the Umbra, but with practice they get better at it and learn that you don't actually need to move to do so. It is just a matter of meditation. I see this as being possible in combat, though it may be significantly harder.<br /> <br /> This is just my interpretation though. So far as I know, the book never states you have to do anything but have a reflection, which the Gift states is no longer needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T17:45:43-08:00","id":834157,"title":"","content":"Stepping Sideways has never (since 2nd edition anyway) required an act of physical movement. While a &quot;medative&quot; it's not necessarily a &quot;calm&quot; or &quot;peaceful&quot;one, all a Garou is doing is reaching out with half of his being and changing state from physical to spirit (or vice versa) the only limitation is gauntlet, reflection and the fact you cannot spend Rage on the same turn you Roll Gnosis. The act of stepping sideways is mentioned as a method that Garou have used to get out of 'concrete shoes' (Glasswalker Wiseguys) and has been used to slip free of the restraints employed by DNA labs and so on and so forth. I would have no issue with it being used in Combat to try and slip a grapple but bear in mind that it requires several successes to get the Instant Step Sideways, otherwise the character is stuck on that action for the minutes listed. Sure they can stop at any time, but stopping also takes their full turn. There are easier ways of getting rid of a nozzie in a grapple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T05:20:23-08:00","id":834379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833691-entering-the-umbra?p=834157#post834157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stepping Sideways has never (since 2nd edition anyway) required an act of physical movement. While a &quot;medative&quot; it's not necessarily a &quot;calm&quot; or &quot;peaceful&quot;one, all a Garou is doing is reaching out with half of his being and changing state from physical to spirit (or vice versa) the only limitation is gauntlet, reflection and the fact you cannot spend Rage on the same turn you Roll Gnosis. The act of stepping sideways is mentioned as a method that Garou have used to get out of 'concrete shoes' (Glasswalker Wiseguys) and has been used to slip free of the restraints employed by DNA labs and so on and so forth. I would have no issue with it being used in Combat to try and slip a grapple but bear in mind that it requires several successes to get the Instant Step Sideways, otherwise the character is stuck on that action for the minutes listed. Sure they can stop at any time, but stopping also takes their full turn. There are easier ways of getting rid of a nozzie in a grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bite his hands off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T07:24:50-08:00","id":834416,"title":"","content":"I think that I would allow the attempt, but I would strictly the time that it would take. <br /> While motion might not be necessary to step sideways, relative calm certainly helps so I would probably also add a penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","user":"lncbill","date":". 02-21-2016, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:54:54-08:00","id":834498,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day. Do what works for your game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I always try to emphasise to my players how not calm their characters are. Even the most centred and zen stargazer or child of Gaia ragabash is far less internally &quot;calm&quot; in their most relaxed and tranquil moments than the most angry human in the world at his or her angriest most volatile moment. Werewolves, always angry, all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T02:02:24-08:00","id":834893,"title":"","content":"WoD:Combat has a mention about stepping sideways in combat situations. Don't have the books with me, but it is in the section where every supernatural natural abilities and their influence on combat is discussed.<br /> <br /> Iirc, being attacked while focusing means no dodge or something like that, and actually a bonus on the attack roll, but a bonus on soak too, since one is already in transition partly...<br /> In general, I would say a person in a grapple would have a difficult time stepping sideways being the grappled party, so difficulty increases and/or willpower expenditure.<br /> On the other hand, it seems a valid tactic to employ 'Parting the Veil' to grapple an enemy an step sideways with him. So, it isn't impossible at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T15:52:57-08:00","id":838834,"title":"","content":"I don't thinks that you should be able to step sideways during combat in most circumstances. If grappled in Chrinos you could slip out by shifting shape suddenly.<br /> <br /> However back on topic I always like the idea that to even get into the umbra you needed a reflective surface. I know it's not canon any more, it's just makes it easier but I always like the idea that it made it harder to step sideways. Not sure how I should treat looking sideways, maybe the reflection warps and instead of showing in what is there in the real world but now show the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T01:16:47-08:00","id":839019,"title":"","content":"You cannot look sideways into the Umbra, only out of the Umbra. Going into the Umbra on combat turns is a thing in Werewolf (just check the comics!), it just requires a modicum of freedom to actually do it (and a damn good roll not to get stuck in the gauntlet)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T04:09:45-08:00","id":839055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833691-entering-the-umbra?p=839019#post839019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot look sideways into the Umbra, only out of the Umbra. Going into the Umbra on combat turns is a thing in Werewolf (just check the comics!), it just requires a modicum of freedom to actually do it (and a damn good roll not to get stuck in the gauntlet)</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the edition. Revised allowed for peeking both ways, although peeking into the umbra was more difficult if the character didn't have some higher level theurge gifts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}